Q: how to change a selections options based on another select option selected (Array)? A: <p>Try This</p>

<p>/// inside your foreach loop</p>

<pre><code>&lt;select id="main[{{$user-&gt;id}}]" class="main"&gt;
   &lt;option value="a"&gt;A&lt;/option&gt;
   &lt;option value="b"&gt;B&lt;/option&gt;
   &lt;option value="c"&gt;C&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/select&gt;

&lt;select id='sub[{{$user-&gt;id}}]' class='sub'&gt;
   &lt;option value="1"&gt;1&lt;/option&gt;
   &lt;option value="2"&gt;2&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/select&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>/// exit foreach loop</p>

<pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
    $('.main').change(function() {
        var options = '';
        if($(this).val() == 'a') {
            options = '&lt;option value="1"&gt;1&lt;/option&gt;';
        }
        else if ($(this).val() == 'b'){
            options = '&lt;option value="2"&gt;2&lt;/option&gt;';
        }

        $(this).next('.sub').html(options);
    });
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Efficiently getting all divisors of a given number A: <p>It seems the best way is to factor an integer and sort its factors, then use recursion to print divisors in order.</p>
<p>This is from sympy's <a href="https://github.com/sympy/sympy/blob/2e489cf4b1438ae134ba98a44a80cc9add1306b0/sympy/ntheory/factor_.py#L1600" rel="nofollow noreferrer">source code</a>:</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>def _divisors(n, proper=False):
    &quot;&quot;&quot;Helper function for divisors which generates the divisors.

    Parameters
    ==========

    n : int
        a nonnegative integer
    proper: bool
        If `True`, returns the generator that outputs only the proper divisor (i.e., excluding n).

    &quot;&quot;&quot;
    if n &lt;= 1:
        if not proper and n:
            yield 1
        return

    factordict = factorint(n)
    ps = sorted(factordict.keys())

    def rec_gen(n=0):
        if n == len(ps):
            yield 1
        else:
            pows = [1]
            for _ in range(factordict[ps[n]]):
                pows.append(pows[-1] * ps[n])
            yield from (p * q for q in rec_gen(n + 1) for p in pows)

    if proper:
        yield from (p for p in rec_gen() if p != n)
    else:
        yield from rec_gen()
</code></pre>
